From 643479f6fd9939594c5ca1857ddc539dc2a90bc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:36:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] shared: E-Ink picture sleep screen on the dozing keyguard

With AOD off the panel keeps SystemUI's dozing keyguard after the
display turns off: black light reveal and scrims, the small clock and
white AOD notification icons. Under the E-Ink keyguard policy
(config_einkKeyguard) make that frame a static white picture page:

- EinkSleepScreenSection (default and split-shade blueprints): while
  the keyguard transition into DOZING has started, a white page with
  the LineageOS logo and "Locked at hh:mm" (sleep start time, system
  12/24-hour format, zh-CN translation) covers the clock and
  smartspace; the AOD notification icons are raised above it. Hidden
  when a transition out of DOZING starts. config_einkSleepScreenShowClock
  keeps the clock instead (no page background).
- Settings.Secure hibreak_sleep_screen_mode selects the mode; only
  "picture" exists and every other value is treated as picture.
- ScrimController: AOD/OFF states with AOD off use an opaque white
  behind scrim and transparent front/notification scrims, unanimated.
- LightRevealScrim end colour white; AOD notification icons black
  without the doze tint; burn-in offsets zero.
- Log tag EinkSleepScreen: "shown locked-at=...", "drawn N ms after
  shown" (frame commit callback) and "hidden".

No display power, window manager or keyguard IPC changes.

Change-Id: I8e865c7d51834c1ffd91cc7d4754efa64d23b34a

Sleep sequence: the page is shown from the start of going to sleep; with AOD off SystemUI controls the screen off (DozeParameters) and DozeScreenState requests the display OFF only after EinkSleepScreenGate saw a presented frame with the visible page (transaction completed + present fence) plus config_einkSleepSettleMs (400), bounded by config_einkSleepTimeoutMs (1500); pulses and AOD states are dropped while ambient display is off. Kill switch persist.debug.hibreak.sleep_screen_wait. Logs: screen-off control: waiting, page presented +N ms, settled/timeout, releasing screen off +N ms (replaces drawn).

Sleep screen modes: the page has translationZ 1000 (also in its constraint set) so clock views, smartspace and sections added or rebuilt later no longer draw over it; the AOD icons are raised above it only in picture mode. clock_1/clock_5/clock_15 show a large black time and the date; EinkSleepScreenRefresher (doze machine part) sets an RTC wakeup alarm at each wall-clock boundary, redraws, requests doze screen ON until the redrawn page is presented and settled (EinkSleepScreenGate.awaitRefresh, config_einkSleepRefreshTimeoutMs 3000) and then OFF, holding the doze wake lock only for that window; time and time zone changes redraw, waking cancels. lockscreen captures the notification shade window (SurfaceFlinger layer capture) at the start of KeyguardService.onStartedGoingToSleep when the lock screen is shown and shows it, otherwise picture. custom shows the image read from the E-Ink app provider (content://net.dianqk.hibreak.eink.sleepscreen/image), FIT_CENTER on white with optional "Locked at" (hibreak_sleep_screen_image_time), otherwise picture. Frames drawn while the display is off no longer count as presented. Logs: refresh (...): display on, refresh: page presented/settled, lock screen captured, custom image loaded/unreadable, (fallback: ...).

Doze on sleep (folded from device/frameworks_base/0003-eink-doze-on-sleep): with AOD and every ambient display feature off the dream manager has no doze component, so the display turned off 20-110 ms after sleep, before the panel finished the sleep page. config_einkDozeOnSleep (default false; set by the product overlay) makes DreamManagerService.getDozeComponent() return the configured doze component also when AmbientDisplayConfiguration.enabled() is false; the double-touch pulse keeps the stock rule. persist.debug.hibreak.sleep_screen_wait=false turns it off (read on every sleep). Logs "doze on sleep: component=..." (EinkSleepScreen) when the component is used only because of this.

Removed the never-overlaid config_einkSleepScreenShowClock branch (the page is always opaque white) and the empty Snapshot.close().
